SUMMARY:AMC Sunday Ecstatic Dance CCLD Fundraiser @WWC w/DJ Bobcat
DESCRIPTION:Asheville Movement Collective\nSunday\, April 26th\n\nCCLD Fun
 draiser at Warren Wilson College\nw/ DJ Bobcat \\(Bob Swoap\\) \\| Support
  Kris Hostikka\n\nIntention: Ready\nReady for the light and the dark.\nFor
  the known and the unknown.\nFor heartbreak\, for joy.\n\nThis collaborati
 ve dance between AMC\, Warren Wilson\, and Emberlight (Center for Consciou
 s Living & Dying) is an invitation to explore how ready we really are.\n\n
 So often\, we feel not ready\,\nand then find ourselves meeting the moment
  anyway.\nSurprising ourselves with our capacity\,\nour community\,\nour l
 ove.\n\n*In the night we sang to storms*\n*Before the peace that breaks at
  dawn*\n*How did we doubt the evening sun*\n*We didn't know we were ready.
 *\n*With the answers at our feet*\n*Will we break the grounds beneath*\n*W
 hat if the dreams were ours to keep*\n*What if the silence said it*\n\\~ 
 Ólafur Arnalds\n\nAbout the DJ\nDJ Bobcat\, Bob Swoap crafts journeys tha
 t invite dancers to deeply connect: with themselves\, others\, nature\, an
 d the music. He layers genres and world rhythms into an emotionally engagi
 ng set. At Warren Wilson College -- where he is professor of psychology an
 d expressive arts therapy -- Bob facilitates ecstatic dance as a part of t
 he community wellness program\, bringing a grounded\, experienced presence
  to the floor. Favorite place to dance: outside at the WWC Pavilion. IG: @
 bob.swoap\n\n\\~\\~\\~\n\n\\*\\* Please note that the dance starts at Warm
  up. The doors close promptly at Opening Circle and people who arrive late
  will be turned away. Please be on time to ensure a safe and secure contai
 ner. \\*\\*\n\nTicket Price: $15-30 or name your price.\nNo one turned awa
 y for lack of funds!\n\n\\~\\~\\~\n\nPre-registration Recommended:\nhttps:
 //ashevillemovementcollective.org/event/\n\nVOLUNTEER!\nWe need volunteers
 . Volunteer and dance for free! Register to volunteer at: [https://ashevil
 lemovementcollective.org/volunteer/](https://ashevillemovementcollective.o
 rg/volunteer/?fbclid=IwZXh0bgNhZW0CMTAAYnJpZBExVTF6aExURExqbndxM3JFUHNydGM
 GYXBwX2lkEDIyMjAzOTE3ODgyMDA4OTIAAR6puHJaet_dJGFESCItA4rMD5vM_RHt9QzUSALul
 ddRTAtGKexRuWuiBE8tDw_aem_vXP_JSWUu1NrAFuKa--PQA)\n\nIMPORTANT ANNOUNCEMEN
 TS:\nDoor will close at the beginning of the opening circle. Please note: 
 NO ENTRY AFTER OPENING CIRCLE BOTH WAVES!\n\nCollective agreements:\n[http
 s://ashevillemovementcollective.org/our-dance/](https://ashevillemovementc
 ollective.org/our-dance/?fbclid=IwZXh0bgNhZW0CMTAAYnJpZBExVTF6aExURExqbndx
 M3JFUHNydGMGYXBwX2lkEDIyMjAzOTE3ODgyMDA4OTIAAR5CSyB7238bGlkEsU_Cg_jsh0446Y
 HLe69W1y3KV5-T6oMaN-7Z3q32wDznUA_aem_wUhim1G2JnrnWxIQYKCcIA)\n\nAbout AMC:
 \nAsheville Movement Collective envisions a world that moves in harmony wh
 ere all are free to be their authentic selves within a loving community. O
 ur mission and aim are to inspire authenticity and healthy community throu
 gh free-form dance by hosting dance waves for personal and community trans
 formation. AMC is a 501(c)(3) nonprofit organization.\n\nSee you on the da
 nce floor!
